Title: Send typed text on AROS
Repository: SDL 3.4.12 with contrib SDL3-3.4.12-aros.diff (contrib 142b3ff4)
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-sdl project
Problem: AROS_TranslateUnicode only had the MorphOS path (IMSGA_UCS4) and returned 0 on AROS, so no SDL_EVENT_TEXT_INPUT was ever sent: text fields received no characters.
Change: Map the key with MapRawKey (with the previous keys, so dead keys combine), keep only printable bytes, convert them from the system character set (ENV:CHARSET, ISO-8859-1 when unset) to UTF-8 with SDL_iconv.
Scope: AROS (src/video/aros)
Upstream: https://github.com/aros-development-team/contrib/pull/91 (open, submitted 2026-11-16)
Verification: Built for mainline x86_64 (GCC 10.5, SDK 20261110); pool v1-1 (nightly 20261113), 2026-11-16: self-test receives SDL_EVENT_TEXT_INPUT for typed letters, Shift and punctuation (US keymap; ISO-8859-2 keymap not yet tried)
Contrib branch: tomaszstaniak/contrib sdl3-text-input 53940520, on contrib master 142b3ff4; built in-tree and checked before/after 2026-11-16 (tests/aros/sdl3-contrib-check.c); PR not opened yet
Removal: when contrib has an equivalent change
